WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.463
What does gate one support?

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:03.387
Three things in NIST's catalog.

3
00:00:03.387 --> 00:00:08.013
Monitoring an external provider's
control compliance on an ongoing basis.

4
00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:12.437
Receiving security alerts and
advisories from outside organizations.

5
00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:17.088
And continuous monitoring, through the
alert path that runs between collections.

6
00:00:17.088 --> 00:00:19.515
The key security indicators are FedRAMP's,

7
00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:23.399
and which record supports which
indicator is the program's mapping.

8
00:00:23.399 --> 00:00:26.896
The security officer keeps the
raw Azure file, the notices,

9
00:00:26.896 --> 00:00:30.028
and the manifest with every
call and its permission,

10
00:00:30.028 --> 00:00:33.888
plus the alert plan and the change
record that approved its hash.

11
00:00:33.888 --> 00:00:38.941
As a side note, Azure Government has its
own CLI cloud and Resource Manager host,

12
00:00:38.941 --> 00:00:43.450
and Learn hasn't stated the table's
availability there in so many words.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.594
Until the reader identity exists,

14
00:00:45.594 --> 00:00:49.575
a person with Reader runs Learn's
own query and keeps the output.

15
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:52.295
And rollback: the collection only reads,

16
00:00:52.295 --> 00:00:55.320
and the alert policy
has a planned rollback.
